(12374, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', '1. New Feature: Turn Quotations into Invoices\nWhat we did: We made it much easier to create an invoice from an approved quotation.\n\nOne-Click Invoice: Admins can now click a button on any \"Approved Quotation\" to create an invoice instantly. You don\'t have to type the client\'s information all over again.\n\nNew Billing Popup: A clean new window opens to collect important details like Payment Mode, GST/PAN, and Bill Type.\n\nNew Pages: Added new sections in the admin panel to handle these invoice steps smoothly.\n\nUI Fix: Fixed a bug where the \"Actions\" menu on the top row of the history list was getting cut off. It now opens downwards so you can see all the options.\n\n2. Cleaning Up the Code (Refactoring)\nWhat we did: We broke down a very large, messy file into smaller, organized pieces.\n\nComponent Splitting: The main \"Create Invoice\" file was too long (1,500 lines!). We split it into two simple parts:\n\nQuotation Mode: For invoices made from quotes.\n\nClient Mode: For invoices made manually.\n\nOrganization: Moved the files to the correct \"Admin\" folder and fixed some naming errors that were causing system glitches.\n\nBetter Performance: Simplified the main dashboard code so it runs more smoothly and is easier for developers to update in the future.', '0', '0', 540, 0, '2026-04-27', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
