(12457, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'new poroject', 'Development', 'Back-End', 'EWA Website\nPerformed API testing during integration and flow validation.\nIdentified and resolved multiple backend and API-related bugs.\nFixed authentication and response handling issues.\nImproved API stability and error handling.\n? Natura Website\nWorked on bug fixes across existing modules.\nResolved UI and functionality-related issues.\nImplemented minor improvements and optimizations.\n? Doaguru Letters Project\nBackend Migration\nMigrated the complete backend from mysql (callback-based) to mysql2/promise.\nConverted callback-based logic into modern async/await architecture.\nRefactored multiple controllers and models for cleaner asynchronous handling.\nBackend Improvements\nShifted DB.js to a promise-based connection pool structure.\nRemoved the redundant DB_promise.js file.\nOptimized query handling and database structure.\nBug Fixes\nFixed the missing db import issue in WarPdfController.js.\nResolved multiple database query execution issues.\nPerformed environment and build artifact cleanup.\nCodebase Cleanup\nRemoved unused dependencies.\nCleaned unnecessary build artifacts (dist.zip).\nImproved import consistency and overall code structure.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-05-06', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12458, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'AI Doctor Assist', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Today, I worked on the AI Doctor application for MedBrainX.com. The login functionality has started working properly, and patient-related data is now being fetched successfully. Some edit/update functionalities are also working now. However, there are still multiple issues remaining because currently the application is only running properly in the web version. When testing it as a real mobile application, several features are not functioning correctly and require further debugging and fixes.\nI also spent a significant amount of time communicating with the A2 Hosting support team regarding hosting setup, configuration, and related technical issues. The discussion and troubleshooting process took longer than expected, but it helped in identifying some important deployment-related problems.\nApart from that, I worked on setting up and testing the load testing environment for the project. However, the load testing setup is currently not working properly due to some system-level issues/faults on my machine. I tried troubleshooting the issue, but it still requires further investigation and fixes before the testing process can run successfully.', '0', '0', 567, 0, '2026-05-06', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
