(12520, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'new poroject', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Backend Architecture and Restructuring\nMVC Implementation: Successfully migrated the backend from the legacy directory to a structured MVC (Model-View-Controller) architecture within the new folder.\n\nModular Routing: Established dedicated routes and controllers for authentication, clients, payments, plans, and staff modules.\n\nEnvironment Configuration: Updated server entry points, database connection strings, and fixed CORS origin mismatches to ensure seamless communication with the frontend.\n\nAuthentication and Security\nRole-Based Access Control: Implemented strict role validation for registration, ensuring users are assigned valid database roles such as admin or receptionist.\n\nSecure Logout: Developed a logout endpoint that clears the JWT token using secure cookie-clearing protocols.\n\nMiddleware Integration: Integrated JWT authentication and role-specific middleware to protect sensitive administrative routes.\n\nStaff and Client Modules\nStaff Management: Built a complete staff module including backend fetching logic and frontend display components.\n\nClient Integration: Integrated Axios for data fetching and implemented the Clients page with optimized loading states and data tables.\n\nStaff Data API: Created a dedicated API to retrieve staff details including status, phone numbers, and roles.\n\nData Integrity and Database Optimization\nQuery Resilience: Refactored the payment retrieval logic using LEFT JOINs and COALESCE functions. This prevents the API from failing when associated user or plan data has been deleted.\n\nError Handling: Implemented graceful fallbacks in the database layer to display \"Deleted User\" or \"Deleted Plan\" instead of returning null results.\n\nFrontend State Management and UI\nContext Optimization: Deconstructed the monolithic AuthContext into four specialized contexts (Staff, Client, Payment, and Plans) to improve application performance and scalability.\n\nModernized UI Components:\n\nEnhanced the Plans modal with new fields for duration units, pricing, and descriptions.\n\nRefactored the Admin Users page to utilize the new StaffContext and modern design layouts.\n\nModular API Layer: Replaced the single API file with a modular service structure, categorizing API calls by their specific domain.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-05-13', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
