(12538, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Summary of Achievements\nToday’s focus was primarily on the end-to-end integration of the YouTube Video Posting service across the Admin and Business Developer (BD) modules, alongside UI refinements for the Quotation and Invoice systems.\n\nKey Tasks Completed\n1. Feature Integration: YouTube Video Posting\nDatabase & Backend:\n\nUpdated saveCalculatorData and updateCalculatorDataById controllers to support the new include_youtube_video_posting column.\n\nModified getController.js to fetch dynamic pricing for YouTube Video Posting from the editing_types table.\n\nCore Logic:\n\nIntegrated include_youtube_video_posting into the dmServiceTotal calculation for both Graphic and Complimentary service flows.\n\nUpdated data mapping in Quotationmode.jsx to ensure seamless service total transitions during Quotation-to-Invoice conversion.\n\nUI/UX Implementation:\n\nAdded dynamic toggle for \"YouTube Video Posting\" as an optional addon under Video Services in AdminCalculator.jsx.\n\nUpdated BDInvoice.jsx and AdminInvoice.jsx to display the specific totals for this new service.\n\n2. UI Standardization & Performance\nHistory & Tables:\n\nStandardized pagination to 10 items per page across Admin and BD history modules.\n\nImplemented internal scrolling using h-[35rem] overflow-auto and applied custom CSS to hide browser-native scrollbars for a cleaner look.\n\nEnhanced History.jsx preview modals to accurately reflect new service totals and final amounts.\n\nLayout Fixes:\n\nAdjusted rowSpan logic in Invoice views to maintain table alignment when the YouTube service row is present.\n\n3. Bug Fixes & Refinement\nConditional Visibility:\n\nImplemented logic in InvoiceServices to hide the thumbnail_creation addon specifically when \"Graphics Design\" is selected, as it is no longer required for that category.\n\nFormatting Updates:\n\nRemoved unnecessary \"=\" symbols from the GST budget display in AdminInvoice.\n\nWrapped percentage values in parentheses within the Management Charges label in Quotations for better readability.\n\nTechnical Stack Impact\nFrontend: React (Context API, Tailwind CSS)\n\nBackend: Node.js, Express\n\nDatabase: MySQL (Sequelize ORM) updates for transaction and invoice tables.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-05-15', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
