(12553, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'FrontEnd ', 'Here is the complete and professional task report translated into structured English, formatted perfectly for your official updates or client/team sharing.\n\nDaily Task Report\nDate: May 19, 2026\n\nDeveloper: Ashish (Full-Stack Web Developer)\n\n1. Workflow Architecture & Feature Design (DM-Calculator & SF Dashboard)\nA major part of today\'s schedule was dedicated to designing a comprehensive project lifecycle, role-based access control, approval matrix, and an automated multi-channel notification system. The complete logic has been mapped out step-by-step below:\n\nPhase 1: Project Initiation & Quotation Flow\nNew Project Lead: As soon as a new project enters the DM-Calculator system, it will be automatically assigned to the Admin by default. This task will immediately populate on the Admin\'s Salesforce (SF) Dashboard, triggering instant notifications via Email and WhatsApp.\n\nQuotation Creation: Any authorized user—whether the Admin or a Manager—can generate the initial quotation. Once created, it is routed to the Super Admin (Company Owner) for internal approval.\n\nClient Dispatch System: Upon Admin approval, a delivery modal/toggle will allow the user to select the preferred channel (Email or WhatsApp) to dispatch the quotation to the client. Contact credentials will be pulled dynamically from the client profile created in DM-Calculator.\n\nPhase 2: Client Response Matrix (4 Core States)\nThe system will dynamically manage four distinct status paths based on client actions:\n\nPending: The status remains \'Pending\' by default. No immediate system action is triggered; the workflow holds until a response is received.\n\nReject: The project/quotation status updates to \'Rejected\' instantly.\n\nChanges: If the client requests revisions, their feedback/remarks are logged, and the system automatically reroutes the project back to Step 2 (Modification & Re-approval).\n\nApprove: Once approved by the client, the project unlocks the next phase: Invoice Generation (Step 5).\n\n???? Note: Real-time notifications for every client movement will be pushed to the Admin, updating their SF Dashboard instantly.\n\nPhase 3: Invoice Processing & Internal Resource Allocation\nInvoice Billing: The system generates the invoice, dispatches it to the client, and sends a confirmation alert to the Admin.\n\nEmployee Data Sync: Admin or Managers will dynamically fetch the real-time employee directory from the Salesforce portal (sf.duaguru.com) into DM-Calculator.\n\nTeam Lead (TL) Assignment: Based on the scope of work and services required, the Admin routes the project to the respective Team Lead. Notifications will simultaneously hit the TL\'s communication channels and the Admin\'s SF Dashboard.\n\nPhase 4: Strategy, Calendar Mapping & Client Sign-off\nProject Owner (PO) Assignment: The TL delegates the project to a specific Project Owner.\n\nPlanning Deliverables: The PO is responsible for uploading two critical deliverables based on the approved quotation: a Project Strategy and a Work/Content Calendar.\n\nApproval & Referral: These deliverables are sent to the Admin for internal approval. Once verified, the Admin refers them to the client via WhatsApp/Email. Upon client sign-off, an \'Approved\' status is flashed across both Admin and PO dashboards, green-lighting the actual execution.\n\n???? Global Feature: Across all stages of approval and delegation, the assigning/approving authority can append custom Remarks, which will be visibly tracked by all upstream and downstream stakeholders.\n\nPhase 5: Dynamic Multi-Task Scheduling & Deadlines\nInteractive Assignment Interface: Clicking the \'Assign\' button in DM-Calculator opens an interface featuring an employee dropdown displaying names alongside their Designations, situated right above an embedded interactive calendar.\n\nBulk Scheduling: Since a single project can encompass multiple services outlined in the quotation, it can have more than one Task Owner. The PO, Admin, or Manager can seamlessly map out different tasks to multiple owners across various dates directly within this unified calendar view.\n\nOmni-Notification Broadcast: Clicking \'Save\' triggers a synchronized broadcast notification to the Task Owner, Admin, Team Lead, and Project Owner. The specific tasks will immediately reflect on the respective Task Owner\'s SF Dashboard.\n\nProactive Deadline Reminders: The dates selected within the calendar are locked as the final task deadlines. A background cron-job service will initiate automated daily countdown reminders to all stakeholders (Task Owner, Admin, TL, PO) starting 4 days prior to the deadline hit.\n\n2. Development, Bug Fixes & Deployment\nAlongside workflow architecture, core production updates and successful deployments were executed today:\n\nDM-Calculator (Core Platform)\nIdentified and patched critical production bugs related to data synchronization.\n\nOptimized invoice rendering engine, user permission states, and dashboard UI linkages.\n\nSuccessfully pushed the stable, tested build to production.\n\nNaturexa.com (Client Project)\nResolved high-priority bugs concerning contact form submission delays and UI positioning issues.\n\nConducted thorough regression testing and successfully deployed the finalized update to the live server.\n\n3. Status Summary\nWorkflow Blueprints & System Logic: 100% Completed & Frozen.\n\nBug Fixing & Deployment (DM-Calculator): Completed & Live.\n\nBug Fixing & Deployment (Naturexa.com): Completed & Live.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-05-19', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
