(12589, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Back-End', 'Daily Work Report — May 25, 2026\nToday\'s work was split across two major tracks: enhancing workflow and payment core features in the DM Calculator Project, and initializing the Mock SF Portal for integration testing.\n\n1. DM Calculator — Workflow & Payment Management\nUpgraded the quotation status tracking, payment processing, and multi-channel communication engine within the DM Calculator ecosystem.\n\n???? Commits & Backend Enhancements (WorkflowController.js)\nWorkflow Controller (6051f38): Enhanced the workflow controller\'s integration with the sendEmails module and optimized error-handling mechanisms for email operations.\n\nQuotation Status & Ledger (eac4aec): Upgraded the quotation state management lifecycle and designed a new workflow_payment_ledger table to log transactions.\n\nProforma Invoice (ab2edd6): Refined the backend logic for proforma invoice generation and streamlined payment processing workflows.\n\n???? Implemented Features\nPayment Tracking: Integrated strict payment validation logic for various transaction methods (UPI, Bank Transfer, Cash, Cheque). Added automatic pending balance calculations and real-time invoice state updates.\n\nGranular Status Tracking: Established a multi-state tracking pipeline ranging from the initial quotation submission (pending) through admin/client evaluations, proforma milestones, up to the final invoice_sent phase.\n\nDual-Channel Notifications & Security: Implemented automated dispatch rules for both Email (sendEmails) and WhatsApp (sendWhatsApp) alerts. Added mandatory x-dm-secret header verification to secure incoming webhooks from Salesforce.\n\n???? Identified Issues & Bugs\nLine 1016 (sfStrategyDecision): Identified an undefined reference bug involving client_id. Needs to be safely extracted from the incoming request body.\n\nOmitted Code Sections: A code review is pending for missing/omitted block structures between lines 978 and 1271.\n\n2. Mock SF Portal — Initialization & Integration Setup\nSuccessfully launched a standalone, mock Salesforce portal environment to safely isolate, test, and simulate incoming and outgoing webhook pipelines with the DM Calculator.\n\n????? Architecture & Core Features\nTech Stack: Standardized on Node.js and Express.js for the server engine, MySQL for the database layer, and a clean, responsive Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS frontend dashboard.\n\nInbound Webhooks: Developed dedicated listening endpoints to process real-time incoming payloads from the DM Calculator (Quotations, Strategies, Project Assignments, and Task Allocations).\n\nOutbound Simulations: Built direct action mechanisms within the interface to mock admin decisions (Approve, Reject, Request Changes) and push task updates straight back to the DM Calculator APIs.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-05-25', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
