(12607, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'new poroject', 'Development', 'FrontEnd ', 'Task Completion Report: ServiceNow Page Redesign\n1. Objective and Overview\nThe ServiceNow page was redesigned by removing heavy raw HTML blocks and replacing them with native WordPress custom elements. The layout was shifted from a dark theme to a premium, clean cream/off-white theme to improve loading speed, backend management, and visual aesthetics.\n\n2. Core Task Breakdown\nTypography Fixes: Removed multi-color gradients from main headings and replaced them with solid corporate colors (Deep Charcoal and Luxury Gold #c5a059). Upgraded sub-heading font-weight from 500 to 600 for better readability.\n\nTheme Shift (Dark to Light): Converted dark backgrounds and deep blue cards into a clean light cream background (#f8fafc) with solid white (#ffffff) cards. Heavy card header gradients were replaced with soft, minimal pastel tints.\n\nInfinite Auto-Scroller: Reengineered the static 4-column service grid into a continuous horizontal scroller. Implemented a lightweight vanilla JavaScript solution for an infinite scrolling loop with a \"Hover-to-Pause\" feature for desktop and mobile touch.\n\nCTA Section Upgrade: Aligned the final section with the new cream/gold palette and added a premium, pill-shaped \"Schedule Free Consultation\" button with smooth hover elevation.\n\n3. Technical Deliverables & Responsiveness\nResponsive Layouts: Adjusted media queries to ensure smooth scaling of typography, grid spacing, and card dimensions across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints.\n\nCode Optimization: Native WordPress element integration backed by optimized, lightweight CSS and JavaScript, eliminating the need for heavy external slider libraries.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-05-30', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
