(12622, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Work Summary\n\nToday’s work focused on stabilizing and refactoring the complete DM ? SF workflow system.\n\nMajor Work Completed\nRefactored strategy workflow architecture\nRemoved automatic SF push during strategy save\nImplemented manual \"Send To Admin\" workflow\nAdded strategy_sent_to_admin workflow handling\nFixed strategy approval synchronization between DM and SF\nStandardized workflow status system across frontend and backend\nAdded centralized WORKFLOW_STATUS architecture\nFixed strategy approval/rejection state handling\nRefactored workflow timeline logic using computeWorkflowStage()\nBackend Improvements\nAdded update-status API\nAdded mark-notifications-read API\nAdded strategy_status and strategy_admin_remark to workflow state\nNormalized workflow API response structure\nFixed pushStrategy() and strategyDecision() status mappings\nAdded admin action middleware security layer\nFrontend Refactor\nConverted frontend to backend-driven workflow state\nRemoved fake local workflow assumptions\nImplemented real setStatus and markAllRead mutations\nReplaced hardcoded localhost URLs with env configuration\nReduced workflow polling frequency\nImproved React Query invalidation flow\nTask Assignment Fixes\nFixed employee_id handling\nRemoved employeeName-as-ID architecture\nNormalized task assignment payload structure\nAdded employee_email support\nFixed task assignment rendering and payload generation\nDashboard Fixes\nFixed SF Admin dashboard workflow conditions\nFixed Project Owner task rendering\nFixed Task Owner assignment handling\nAdded null safety across dashboards\nFixed stale workflow state issues\nUI & Workflow Improvements\nExpanded STATUS_TONE support for all workflow statuses\nFixed workflow timeline rendering\nImproved status label consistency\nFixed task and strategy schema mismatches\nFinal Outcome\n\nThe workflow system is now more stable, synchronized, backend-driven, and scalable across both DM and SF platforms.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-06-02', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12623, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'AI Doctor Assist', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', '**Daily Work Update**\n\nToday, I continued working on the HMS module integration and architecture improvements. A significant portion of the work was focused on strengthening the backend structure by creating and integrating multiple controllers for core HMS functionalities, including Patient Management, Staff Management, Room Management, OPD Operations, and Appointment Management. These controllers were connected with the respective services and business logic to ensure proper data handling and workflow execution.\n\nI also implemented and configured middleware layers such as Authentication, Validation, Error Handling, and Logging to improve application security, request validation, debugging capabilities, and overall maintainability.\n\nAdditionally, I worked on organizing and connecting various route modules across the HMS system, ensuring that all APIs are properly mapped and accessible through a structured routing architecture. Special attention was given to verifying internal navigation and module connectivity to ensure smooth communication between different HMS components.\n\nA major part of today\'s effort was dedicated to testing end-to-end integration, validating API flows, reviewing internal routing between modules, and confirming that newly added controllers, middleware, and routes are functioning correctly within the overall system architecture.\n\nOverall, today\'s progress further strengthened the HMS backend foundation by improving module connectivity, enhancing application structure, and ensuring that critical workflows are properly integrated and operational.\n', '0', '0', 334, 0, '2026-06-02', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0),
