(12632, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'AI Doctor Assist', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Today, I focused on expanding and strengthening the HMS backend architecture by implementing new modules and improving system-level integration. A major part of the work involved developing the Ambulance Management module, including the creation of the Ambulance Controller, Ambulance Routes, and Ambulance Page, ensuring proper connectivity between the frontend interface and backend APIs.\nI also worked on configuring core backend infrastructure components such as database connectivity through db.js, API configuration and integration through api.js, and authentication handling using authMiddleware.js. These improvements helped establish a more secure and maintainable application structure while ensuring consistent communication between different HMS modules.\nAdditionally, I continued enhancing the system\'s domain architecture by organizing module-level integrations and validating interactions between controllers, routes, middleware, and frontend pages. Special attention was given to maintaining a scalable project structure and ensuring that newly introduced modules align correctly with the overall HMS workflow.\nThe day also included integration testing and verification of API endpoints, authentication flows, and module connectivity to confirm that all newly implemented components function correctly within the Hospital Management System.\nOverall, today\'s progress strengthened the HMS foundation by introducing the Ambulance Management workflow, improving core application configuration, enhancing security mechanisms, and ensuring smooth integration across backend and frontend components.', '0', '0', 515, 0, '2026-06-04', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12633, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Bug Fixed ', 'Work was carried out to resolve multiple issues related to duplicate invoice functionality. The fixes mainly focused on:\n\nInvoice data not loading properly\nIncorrect amount calculations\nDuplicate invoice update issues\nRemoval of unnecessary API-related code\n1. Duplicate Invoice Data Fetch Issue\nProblem\n\nDuplicate invoices were not loading the required data correctly after duplication.\n\nCause\n\nThe required client information was not being returned during the duplicate invoice process, which caused incorrect routing and prevented invoice data from loading.\n\nResolution\n\nThe missing client information was added to the duplicate invoice response so that invoice data can now load correctly after duplication.\n\nStatus\n\nCompleted\n\n2. Amount Showing as 0 After Adding New Service\nProblem\n\nWhen adding a new service to a duplicated invoice, the total amount was getting saved as 0.\n\nCause\n\nThere was a mismatch in the invoice save process, causing amount values to shift incorrectly during data insertion.\n\nResolution\n\nThe missing field was added to the save process to ensure all values are stored in the correct order and amounts are calculated properly.\n\nStatus\n\nCompleted\n\n3. Duplicate Invoice Edit Not Saving Updated Amount\nProblem\n\nWhile editing duplicated invoices, updated amount values were not being saved.\n\nCause\n\nThe update process was stopping early when certain records were not found, even though duplicate invoice data still existed in another table.\n\nRequired Resolution\n\nThe unnecessary stop condition needs to be removed so the duplicate invoice update process can continue successfully.\n\nStatus\n\nPending\n\n4. Removal of Unused API Call\nProblem\n\nAn unnecessary API call existed in the frontend which was not available in the backend and was never functioning correctly.\n\nResolution\n\nThe unused API-related code was removed and replaced with a simpler fallback handling method.\n\nStatus\n\nCompleted', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-06-04', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
