(12641, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Bug Fixed ', 'Detailed Task Report — DM Calculator Bug Fixes & Improvements\n\nThis report outlines the technical issues identified in the DM Calculator application along with the frontend, backend, and database-level fixes implemented to resolve them.\n\n1. Ads Campaign Budget Calculator — Duplicate Amount Entry Fix\n\n[!WARNING]\nIssue Identified\nWhen adding an amount to an already existing Ads service (such as Google Ads or Meta Ads), the system was creating duplicate records instead of updating the existing service amount.\n\nRoot Cause\nBackend save logic lacked validation for existing service entries.\nEvery save request triggered a fresh INSERT query regardless of existing records.\nSolution Implemented\nInvestigated and refactored the backend save logic in:\nserver/controller/controller.js\nImplemented Upsert Logic (Update or Insert):\nIf the same client, service, and category already exist:\nUpdate the existing amount\nOtherwise:\nCreate a new entry\nResult\n\n? Duplicate service entries are no longer created\n? Existing service amounts now update correctly\n\n2. Total Budget Calculation Bug — String Concatenation Issue\n\n[!WARNING]\nIssue Identified\nThe \"Total Ads Budget\" calculation was incorrect because numeric values were being treated as strings.\n\nExample\n\"100\" + \"200\" = \"100200\"\n\ninstead of:\n\n100 + 200 = 300\nRoot Cause\nAmount values were received as strings from the API/UI.\nMathematical operations were performed without numeric conversion.\nSolution Implemented\nAdded parseFloat() wrapping to all total calculation logic.\nUpdated Files\nclient/src/Admin/InvoiceAds.jsx\nclient/src/Admin/AdsCampaignCalculator.jsx\nResult\n\n? Accurate mathematical calculations\n? Total budget values now display correctly\n\n3. Invoice Table Fix for Optional Add-on Services\n\n[!WARNING]\nIssue Identified\nOptional add-on services such as:\n\nThumbnail Creation\nContent Posting\nYouTube Video Posting\n\nwere not appearing properly in generated invoice totals.\n\nRoot Cause\nadditionalServiceData was not integrated into the invoice rendering flow.\nAdd-on totals were skipped during invoice aggregation.\nSolution Implemented\nUpdated:\nclient/src/Admin/AdminInvoice.jsx\nIntegrated additionalServiceData into the graphicData rendering logic.\nBuilt aggregation logic to:\nMerge optional add-ons into dedicated invoice rows\nPrevent fragmented or duplicate rows\nResult\n\n? Optional services now appear correctly in invoices\n? Invoice totals are properly aggregated\n? Cleaner invoice table structure\n\n4. YouTube Video Posting — Save & Display Fix\n\n[!WARNING]\nIssue Identified\n\n\"YouTube Video Posting\" selection was:\nNot saving in the database\nNot appearing in invoices\nIncorrect label displayed:\n\"YouTube Channel Growth & Optimization\"\n\ninstead of:\n\n\"YouTube Video Posting\"\n4.1 Database-Level Fix\nRoot Cause\n\nThe addtional_service table was missing the required column.\n\nSQL Fix Executed\nALTER TABLE addtional_service \nADD COLUMN include_youtube_video_posting varchar(255) NOT NULL DEFAULT \'0\' \nAFTER include_thumbnail_creation;\nResult\n\n? Database schema updated successfully\n\n4.2 Backend Fixes\nUpdated Files\nserver/controller/controller.js\nserver/controller/updateController.js\nFixes Applied\nIn saveAdditionalData\nAdded:\ninclude_youtube_video_posting\nUpdated:\nRequest body destructuring\nINSERT query\nIn updateAdditionalDataById\n\nDiscovered a critical issue where optional add-on fields were entirely missing from the SQL SET clause.\n\nAdded:\n\ninclude_content_posting\ninclude_thumbnail_creation\ninclude_youtube_video_posting\nResult\n\n? Add-on values now save and update correctly\n\n4.3 Frontend Fixes\nUpdated File\nclient/src/Admin/AdminInvoice.jsx\nFixes Applied\nUpdated getServiceDisplayName() logic\nCorrected invoice labels to display:\n\"YouTube Video Posting\"\n\ninstead of:\n\n\"YouTube Channel Growth & Optimization\"\nResult\n\n? Correct service naming in invoice UI\n? Proper invoice rendering\n\n5. Edit Mode YES/NO Toggle Button Fix\n\n[!WARNING]\nIssue Identified\nWhile editing saved services using the ?? Edit button:\n\nYES/NO toggle buttons became disabled\nUsers could not modify:\nThumbnail Creation\nContent Posting\nYouTube Video Posting\n5.1 Disabled Button Restriction Fix\nRoot Cause\n\nButtons contained:\n\ndisabled={!!editId}\n\nand guarded click handlers:\n\n!editId\n\nwhich blocked interaction during edit mode.\n\nSolution Implemented\n\nRemoved these restrictions from:\n\nAdminInvoice.jsx\nAdminCalculator.jsx\nInvoiceCalculation.jsx\nResult\n\n? Toggle buttons are now editable in edit mode\n\n5.2 State Overwrite Prevention Fix\nRoot Cause\n\nuseEffect() hooks were resetting toggle values with default states immediately after loading edit data from the database.\n\nSolution Implemented\n\nAdded edit guards:\n\nif (editId) return;\n\ninside relevant useEffect() hooks.\n\nResult\n\n? Existing DB values are preserved during editing\n? No unwanted state resets\n\n5.3 Key Generation Mismatch Fix\nRoot Cause\n\nLabels containing question marks (?) generated incorrect state keys.\n\nExample\n\"YouTube Video Posting?\"\n\ncaused state mismatch issues.\n\nSolution Implemented\n\nApplied:\n\n.replace(/\\?/g, \"\")\n\nduring:\n\nButton mapping\nhandleEdit key generation\nResult\n\n? State keys now match database fields correctly\n? Toggle values sync properly\n\n???? Affected Files Summary\nBackend Files\nserver/controller/controller.js\nserver/controller/updateController.js\nFrontend Files\nclient/src/Admin/AdminInvoice.jsx\nclient/src/Admin/AdminCalculator.jsx\nclient/src/Admin/InvoiceCalculation.jsx\nclient/src/Admin/InvoiceAds.jsx\nclient/src/Admin/AdsCampaignCalculator.jsx\n? Final Outcome\n\nAfter implementing the above fixes:\n\nDuplicate service entries were eliminated\nBudget calculations became accurate\nOptional add-on services now save and render correctly\nInvoice tables display proper aggregated totals\nYouTube Video Posting functionality works end-to-end\nEdit mode toggle buttons function correctly\nDatabase, backend, and frontend states remain fully synchronized', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-06-05', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
