(12695, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'HMS', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Patient Discharge Management Enhancement\nDesigned and implemented a complete Patient Discharge Workflow integrated with the Hospital Management System, enabling nurses to digitally process patient discharge records with proper authorization and tracking.\nDeveloped a dedicated Nurse Discharge Summary Module allowing nursing staff to:\nSelect admitted patients.\nRecord discharge date & time.\nUpdate patient condition at discharge.\nEnter doctor recommendations and follow-up instructions.\nGenerate and store discharge sign-off records.\nImplemented automated backend logic to ensure real-time patient lifecycle management, where:\nPatient status is automatically updated from \"Admitted\" ? \"Discharged\".\nHospital occupancy records remain synchronized across all modules.\nBed allocation is automatically released upon discharge.\nEnhanced system-wide data consistency by enabling automatic room and bed availability updates, ensuring accurate hospital resource management without manual intervention.\nIntegrated real-time synchronization mechanisms using periodic polling, allowing Reception, IPD, and Nurse dashboards to instantly reflect discharge actions across the platform.\nIPD Enquiry & Reporting Improvements\nExtended the IPD Admission Management APIs to retrieve and expose historical discharge information by integrating discharge records with admission datasets.\nImplemented backend-level joins between IPD Admissions and Nurse Discharge History tables to provide consolidated patient admission-discharge visibility.\nAdded a dedicated Discharge Date column within the In-Patient Enquiry (IPD Search) interface, allowing hospital staff to instantly identify discharged patients and their discharge timelines.\nImproved patient record transparency by displaying both Admission Date and Discharge Date within enquiry reports and patient tracking screens.\nFixed data mapping inconsistencies in the Patient Details Modal where discharge information was previously displaying incorrect values, ensuring accurate medical record presentation.\nAdded support for both MySQL Database Mode and JSON Database Fallback Mode, ensuring discharge information remains available across multiple deployment environments.\nOperational Impact\nReduced manual tracking effort for discharged patients.\nImproved hospital bed utilization visibility.\nEnhanced accuracy of patient movement records.\nEnabled better auditability and reporting of patient admission-to-discharge history.\nStrengthened overall Hospital Management System workflow automation and data integrity.', '0', '0', 510, 0, '2026-06-13', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12696, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'new poroject', 'Development', 'FrontEnd ', 'Daily Task Report – BharatRoofers / Siara Properties Project\n\n1. React Build Error Resolution (\"SingleProperty.jsx\")\n\nIssue\n\n- React client build process repeatedly failed with a parsing error:\n  - \"Parsing error: Unexpected character \'\'\"\n- The issue originated from a corrupted \"SingleProperty.jsx\" file containing invalid/null byte characters.\n- Even after replacing the file, the error continued because Webpack was serving the cached corrupted version.\n\nWork Done\n\n- Verified and restored the file integrity.\n- Cleared the Webpack cache directory.\n- Restarted the React development server to force a fresh build.\n\nResult\n\n- Build process completed successfully.\n- Application compiled without any parsing or cache-related errors.\n\n---\n\n2. Navbar Layout & Logo Consistency Improvements\n\nIssue\n\n- Older pages such as About and Properties had inconsistent navbar spacing.\n- Logo alignment differed from the newly designed homepage.\n- Navigation elements appeared too close to the screen edges.\n\nWork Done\n\n- Added consistent horizontal padding (\"0 5%\") to the navbar component.\n- Standardized logo positioning across all pages.\n- Matched navbar styling with the new homepage design.\n\nResult\n\n- Uniform navigation experience across the entire website.\n- Improved visual balance and responsiveness.\n\n---\n\n3. Branding Update Across Client & Admin Panel\n\nIssue\n\n- Admin panel was still displaying outdated branding assets.\n- Existing favicon and logo did not match the new Siara Properties identity.\n\nWork Done\n\n- Created and implemented a new SVG favicon based on the “SP” brand mark.\n- Added favicon support to both Client and Admin applications.\n- Updated admin page title to reflect the new branding.\n- Replaced old image-based logos with a modern text-based \"SP Siara Properties\" logo.\n- Updated branding in:\n  - Admin Navbar\n  - Mobile Sidebar\n  - Offcanvas Navigation Components\n\nResult\n\n- Consistent branding across both client-facing and admin applications.\n- Improved professional appearance and brand recognition.\n\n---\n\n4. Services Page UI & Animation Enhancements\n\nIssue\n\n- Services page lacked the premium animation experience available on other redesigned pages.\n- User interactions felt comparatively static.\n\nWork Done\n\n- Implemented GSAP ScrollTrigger-based parallax effects on hero/banner sections.\n- Added clip-path reveal animations for section headings.\n- Added smooth fade-in and slide-up effects for content sections.\n- Created an animated scroll indicator for better user guidance.\n- Enhanced service cards and area cards with scale and opacity transitions.\n- Enabled smooth scrolling navigation for CTA buttons using Lenis.\n- Added subtle section dividers to improve content separation and readability.\n\nResult\n\n- More engaging and interactive user experience.\n- Improved visual flow and page aesthetics.\n- Consistent premium animation style across the website.\n\n---\n\nOverall Outcome\n\n- Fixed critical build and compilation issues.\n- Standardized UI layout and navigation styling.\n- Completed migration to Siara Properties branding across client and admin platforms.\n- Enhanced the Services page with modern GSAP animations and smooth scrolling interactions.\n- Improved overall visual consistency, user experience, and application stability.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-06-13', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
