(12712, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'new poroject', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', '# Daily Task Report – June 15, 2026\n\n## Proposal Workflow Development\n\nWorked on building and improving the new Proposal-based workflow for the project. The system is being designed to handle the complete process from proposal creation to payment tracking and invoice generation.\n\n## Database & Backend Updates\n\nCreated the required database structure for proposals, proforma invoices, and payment records. Updated backend APIs and controllers to support proposal management, proposal sharing, PDF generation, and payment handling.\n\nImproved the existing PDF generation system so it can be reused across different document types while maintaining a consistent layout and design.\n\n## Proposal Builder\n\nDeveloped the Proposal Builder for both Admin and Business Developer panels. Added support for creating detailed proposals, managing pricing information, adding proposal content, and including Terms & Conditions.\n\nAlso added options to send proposals directly to clients through Email and WhatsApp.\n\n## Client & Proforma Integration\n\nIntegrated proposal management inside client profile screens, making it easier to create and manage proposals for individual clients.\n\nAdded support for generating Proforma Invoices from approved proposals and connected proposal workflows with the invoice generation process.\n\n## Payment Tracking\n\nBuilt a dedicated payment management module for proposals. Added functionality to record payments, track transaction details, and manage TDS calculations.\n\nThe system now helps monitor proposal-related payments more efficiently.\n\n## Graphify Analysis\n\nAnalyzed the entire codebase using Graphify and generated project reports and visualizations to better understand component relationships, dependencies, and workflow structures.\n\nThis helped in planning future improvements and proposal workflow integration.\n\n## Routing & System Updates\n\nUpdated application routes and navigation to support the newly developed proposal modules while maintaining proper access control for Admin and Business Developer users.\n\n## Status\n\nCompleted development, integration, testing, and analysis tasks related to the Proposal Workflow. All changes have been committed and pushed successfully.\n', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-06-15', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12713, 129, 'Ritik Brown', 'DOAGURU', 'sales', 'sales', 'Called On Total 60 Numbers, Including Clinics And Business Owners, Of Jabalpur, Also Worked on Ad Content For DOA Sales, One Positive response from Doctor to meet on saturday as he is out of town', '0', '0', 270, 0, '2026-06-16', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12714, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', '1. Summary of Today\'s Work\nToday, we fixed important bugs in the Proposal and Proforma Invoice system, added new delete features, made PDF downloads faster, and cleaned up the code to make it easier to manage.\n\n2. Bugs That We Fixed\nFixed the \"Action Failed\" Error: Before, clicking \"Create Invoice\" caused an error because some background information was missing. We fixed this, and it works perfectly now.\n\nFixed Wrong Link (API Route): The frontend was sending data to the wrong URL. We updated it to the correct backend URL (/auth/api/calculator/proforma).\n\nFixed Data Format: The system now sends the exact data the server needs (Proposal ID, Client ID, Base Amount, and Total Amount).\n\nPrevented PDF Crashes: Fixed a backend bug where the system would crash if any data or text was missing while making a PDF.\n\n3. New Features Added\nDelete Proposal Button: You can now permanently delete a proposal directly from the action menu.\n\nDelete Proforma Button: Added a delete button next to the Payment History table so you can remove wrong proforma entries easily.\n\nQuick PDF Download: Added a \"Download PDF\" button right inside the main menu so you can download files instantly without extra clicks.\n\n4. Code Cleanup (Making it Simple)\nThe History.jsx file was getting too big and messy. We split it into 4 smaller, clean files to make it easy to update in the future:\n\nProposalTable: Handles active proposals.\n\nLegacyQuotationTable: Shows old quotations (Read-Only).\n\nProposalActions: Handles buttons like edit, delete, and download.\n\nProformaManagerModal: The new popup window to manage all payments.\n\n5. Project Health Status\nWe ran a code check tool (Graphify) to see how the project looks:\n\nEverything is Connected: The project has 123 files, and all files are perfectly linked with zero broken code links.\n\nMain Files: The Database (db), the Dashboard, and the PDF generators are the main pillars holding the code together.\n\n6. Next Steps\nClean Up Messy Areas: A few old parts of the backend code are a bit messy. We need to split them into smaller, cleaner files in the next updates.\n\nKeep Checking Code: Keep running the health check tool regularly so the code does not break as the project grows', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-06-16', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12715, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'Scheduler for events', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Database Setup: Managed drop-and-recreate MySQL database initializer initDb.js that seeds tables (employees, reminders, notifications, reminder_employees) with mock data automatically.\nREST APIs: Implemented CRUD API endpoints for rules, unread notifications tracker, logs, and a dashboard statistics counter.\nCron Daemon: Designed a 1-minute interval background service in Node.js that processes timezone offsets, evaluates Do Not Disturb (DND) periods, and updates status flags.\nSMTP Email Provider: Configured email delivery integration using Nodemailer SMTP, complete with environment variables setup.\nWhatsApp Provider: Added real-time WhatsApp message delivery using Twilio API (via native Node.js fetch).\nDelivery Fallbacks: Implemented fallback simulated console logging if API keys or SMTP secrets are not provided in .env.\nSticky Navigation: Created a sticky, glassmorphism header navigation bar with live indicator badges for unread in-app alerts.\nHorizontal Layout Form: Designed a horizontal-first scheduling form (ReminderForm.jsx) where fields align side-by-side on wide displays and wrap on smaller screens.\nControl Dashboard: Built a premium white-themed analytics dashboard (ReminderDashboard.jsx) complete with statistics cards, search query bars, and filter tabs.', '0', '0', 515, 0, '2026-06-16', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
