(12735, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', '# Task Report – Proposal to Proforma Workflow Improvements\n\n## Objective\n\nThe objective was to fix the Proposal to Proforma generation workflow where Ads Services and DM Services were not being displayed separately. Additionally, Proposal totals and Proforma totals were not matching because of inconsistent handling of Ads service calculations and rendering.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Proposal Data Persistence Fix\n\n### Issue\n\nWhile saving a proposal, Ads Campaign details such as Budget, Amount, Percentage, and Charge Amount were not being stored in the `pricing_table_json`. Only basic pricing values were being saved, causing loss of important Ads-related information.\n\n### Solution\n\nUpdated `ProposalBuilder.jsx` (`syncCustomServices`) to preserve complete Ads metadata including:\n\n* Budget\n* Amount\n* Percentage\n* Charge Amount\n\nThis information is now stored along with the proposal data and remains available throughout the entire workflow.\n\n### Result\n\nAds-related information is no longer lost during proposal creation and is available for Proforma generation, Invoice rendering, and PDF printing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Single Source of Truth for Ads Classification\n\n### Issue\n\nAds services were being identified differently across multiple components, leading to inconsistent behavior.\n\n### Solution\n\nStandardized Ads identification using:\n\n```js\nsource === \"custom_ads\"\n```\n\nThis is now the primary and consistent method for identifying Ads services across the workflow.\n\n### Result\n\nImproved consistency, reduced complexity, and eliminated classification conflicts.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Shared Utility Implementation\n\n### Issue\n\nService classification and Ads calculation logic existed in multiple locations, creating duplication and increasing maintenance effort.\n\n### Solution\n\nCreated a shared utility:\n\n`client/src/utils/proformaPricing.js`\n\nThe utility centralizes:\n\n* DM Service classification\n* Ads Service classification\n* Ads calculation handling\n* Legacy proposal support\n\n### Result\n\nAll screens now use the same logic, ensuring consistent behavior throughout the application.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Legacy Proposal Compatibility Support\n\n### Issue\n\nOlder proposals contained Ads services but did not store fields such as Budget, Percentage, and Charge Amount.\n\n### Solution\n\nImplemented fallback handling for older proposals:\n\n* Budget is derived from available pricing values.\n* Missing Percentage and Charge values are displayed as \"N/A\".\n* No runtime errors occur when opening historical proposals.\n\n### Result\n\nPreviously generated proposals continue to work without requiring any database migration or manual updates.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Proforma Preview Modal Enhancement\n\n### Issue\n\nWhen generating a Proforma from a Proposal, all services were displayed within a single table, making Ads services difficult to identify.\n\n### Solution\n\nUpdated `History.jsx` to use the shared classification utility and separate services into:\n\n* DM Services\n* Ads Services\n\n### Result\n\nThe Proforma Preview now displays clear and organized service breakdowns using dedicated tables.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Proposal and Proforma Total Alignment\n\n### Issue\n\nProposal totals and Proforma totals were not matching because Ads rows were being handled differently during rendering.\n\n### Solution\n\nAligned the Proposal-based Proforma rendering logic with the actual Proposal pricing structure and removed the mismatch introduced during Ads display calculations.\n\n### Result\n\nProposal Total, Proforma Preview Total, and Final Proforma Total now remain consistent throughout the workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Final Proforma and PDF Rendering Fix\n\n### Issue\n\nThe final Proforma page and printed PDF were not displaying Ads services separately even when the preview was correct.\n\n### Solution\n\nUpdated `AdminInvoice.jsx` to use the same shared utility used by the preview modal.\n\n### Result\n\nThe following views now display identical information:\n\n* Proposal Preview\n* Proforma Preview\n* Final Proforma Page\n* Printed PDF\n\n---\n\n## 8. Workflow Consistency Validation\n\n### Validation Performed\n\nThe complete workflow was tested and validated:\n\n1. Proposal Creation\n2. Proposal Save\n3. Generate Proforma\n4. Proforma Preview\n5. Final Proforma View\n6. Print / PDF Generation\n\n### Result\n\nData integrity, service classification, and totals remain consistent across every stage of the process.\n\n---\n\n## Final Outcome\n\n* Ads Services and DM Services are displayed in separate sections.\n* Ads metadata is preserved from Proposal creation through final PDF generation.\n* Legacy proposals continue to function correctly.\n* Proposal totals and Proforma totals remain synchronized.\n* Shared utility implementation eliminates duplicated logic.\n* No changes were made to financial calculations, payment workflows, or legacy transaction-based Proforma generation.\n* Proposal ? Proforma ? PDF workflow is now fully synchronized and consistent.\n', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-06-18', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
