(12744, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', '# Task Report - June 19, 2026\n\n## Proposal to Proforma Invoice Pricing Pipeline Fix\n\nA bug was fixed in the data conversion pipeline from Proposals to Proforma Invoices. When a user selected a predefined plan containing an Ads Campaign, the system failed to classify it as an Advertising Service because the plan data lacked a service type label. This misclassification caused incorrect pricing and budget calculations on the final invoice view. To fix this, the classification logic in proformaPricing.js was updated to check the service name attribute as well. Testing confirmed that Ads Campaigns from predefined plans are now correctly categorized and calculated on the Proforma Invoice page.\n\n## Dead Code Removal\n\nAn unused component named ProposalPricingBuilder.jsx was located in the project files. Although its functionality had already been moved directly into the main ProposalBuilder.jsx component, its import statement was still active in the codebase. The unused import was removed to keep the file clean, and a warning comment was added inside ProposalPricingBuilder.jsx to mark it as dead code to avoid future development confusion.\n\n## Section Eleven Refactoring and Crash Resolution\n\nSection 11 was modified to completely remove the rigid Terms and Conditions checkbox templates while keeping the entire Notes management functionality functional. An initial cleanup pass caused a frontend crash because the layout tree tried to render the checkboxes after their state data array was deleted. This runtime loop error was resolved by removing the orphaned rendering blocks from the JSX file. The save function was also updated to explicitly send empty arrays for terms, preventing empty reference errors.\n\n## Admin and Business Developer Portal Synchronization\n\nTo maintain consistency and prevent interface crashes across different staff roles, the identical Section 11 cleanups were applied to the Business Developer portal. All state tracking definitions, automated data fetching functions, and checkbox layout containers were removed from ProposalBuilderBD.jsx. Both portals now use the same updated structure and send uniform empty data fields to the backend application layers.\n\n## Database and PDF Generation Compatibility\n\nThe backend database storage and server-side PDF generation utilities were verified to ensure safe data handling. The proposalController.js script was preserved without schema modifications to protect backward compatibility. For new proposals, the database safely records empty arrays for the removed checkboxes, and the PDF engine automatically skips printing the checklist lines while still rendering the selected text notes under the header. Older historical proposals containing existing checklist records continue to compile and print perfectly without layout degradation.\n\n## Current System Stability Status\n\nThe entire application builds successfully without any compilation errors, syntax warnings, or broken references. The local frontend crash has been fully resolved. The entire system lifecycle covering proposal initialization, backend data saving, proforma invoice generation, and PDF document rendering is operating in a stable and production-ready state.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-06-19', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
