(12890, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'Task Efforts and Sales Funnel Project', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Letter Integrated with SF\n\nDismantled Screen Constraints: Restructured letters.css to remove rigid height limits, enabling fluid scrolling and 98% widescreen centering across all letters screens.\nVisual Hierarchy Refinements: Removed redundant subtext and bolded critical target terms (e.g., offer letter, warning letter) across all form modules.\nTablet Responsive Overhaul: Upgraded all navbar breakpoints from mobile-only (md/sm) to tablet-first (lg - 1024px) and added a functional hamburger menu for tablets.\nSmooth Entry Animations: Resolved the dropdown animation jump by building a custom @keyframes fadeInUpCentered translation matrix, ensuring seamless, snap-free dropdown loads.\nProduction Build Validation: Ran clean production compilations to ensure the code remains stable and production-ready.', '0', '0', 508, 0, '2026-06-30', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12891, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Daily Task Report (June 30, 2026)\n\nThis report provides a comprehensive summary of all the tasks, architectural shifts, bug fixes, database migrations, and UI/UX enhancements completed today across the DM Calculator system.\n\nFeature Additions and Enhancements\n\n1.1 History Hub Expansion\nA new Balance Proforma tab has been added to the History Hub to filter and isolate proformasinvoices with pending or partial payments. It features a dynamic preview mechanism that opens the correct billing view. Additionally, an independent global Payment History tab has been created, powered by a newly registered backend endpoint that aggregates all historical client transaction records across the system. Table layouts within these views have been optimized to stack client details and organization names cleanly.\n\n1.2 Installment Based Rolling Invoice Architecture\nThe invoicing system has transitioned from an aggregate overwrite model to a sequential ledger snapshot model. When a client makes an installment payment, the system creates an isolated, point-in-time invoice snapshot instead of updating a cumulative row. This architecture uses a contextual routing system that reads an optional transaction identifier from the URL parameters. If this identifier is present, the interface bypasses cumulative histories to display the historical data state frozen at that specific payment milestone.\n\n1.3 Clickable Historical Ledger Links\nTo support the multi-invoice snapshot system, the Payment History data table has been upgraded with interactive navigation. Dates within the transaction lines are now rendered as unique hyperlinks mapped to individual milestone transaction IDs. Clicking a historical payment line opens that specific installment\'s exact point-in-time invoice snapshot in a new browser tab for viewing or printing.\n\n1.4 Proforma Invoice Modal Refactoring\nThe inline proforma creation logic has been completely decoupled from the view layouts and extracted into a standalone, reusable modal component. This modular component has been integrated across both the standard history views and the global proposal listings, allowing users to generate new proformas natively from multiple context screens using a standardized action hook.\n\n1.5 Admin Invoice Premium Redesign\nThe bottom financial summary and layout block of the administrative invoice interface has been entirely overhauled to match a premium enterprise application standard. The interface splits the layout into a card-based structure allocating thirty-eight percent of the horizontal screen space to banking and authorization details, and sixty-two percent to structured financial status containers. This panel uses clear background color coding and visual hierarchy to group metrics seamlessly.\n\nBug Fixes and System Stability\n\n2.1 Invoice Service Deduplication\nFixed an engineering bug where Ads Campaign services were duplicating on specific invoice generations. This was resolved by stripping the timestamp field from the underlying MySQL union query, which restored standard database deduplication behavior across the rows.\n\n2.2 Classification of Service Charges\nResolved a data-rendering issue where specific operational service charges failed to appear on final generated Tax Invoices. All fetched items are now channeled through a dedicated classification utility that maps, structures, and prepends explicit descriptive category prefixes to all rendering tables.\n\n2.3 Dropdown State Reset Fix\nFixed a UI glitch where the proposal selection dropdown within the new proforma builder would unexpectedly clear its state on parent component updates. This was fixed by implementing an initialization reference flag to prevent accidental triggers during state re-renders.\n\n2.4 Missing Transaction Columns and Calculations\nAddressed a system crash during payment logging caused by a missing database property reference. In tandem with database updates, the backend logic was updated to generate a compound unique identifier matching the original proforma tracking sequence combined with a millisecond timestamp. This guarantees that line item pricing records are duplicated accurately into historical graphic, ads, and complimentary tables for every distinct payment snapshot.\n\n2.5 Milestone Rolling Math Realignment\nCorrected the mathematical calculations inside the point-in-time invoice preview. The outstanding balance formula now reads directly from specific snapshot parameters rather than calculating global aggregate balances. It ensures that the current balance subtracts the isolated gross payment received from the previous rolling milestone, while displaying the exact, isolated tax deduction for that transaction alone without cumulative bleeding.\n\nDatabase Schema Migrations\n\n3.1 Table Invoice Migrations\nA structural database alteration was applied to the live invoice schema to support milestone tax tracking. A new decimal column for isolated tax deductions was appended immediately following the existing tax fields, configured to preserve historical points of data safely.\n\n3.2 Table Proposal Payment Records Migrations\nA transaction identifier column was added to the payment logging schema to link receipt records directly to their corresponding milestone invoice entries. A dedicated database index was applied to this column to optimize structural queries, row joins, and retrieval speeds.\n\nCommits Pushed Today\n\n4.1 Commit d7e9354\nTime: 19:35\nMessage: feat(invoice): redesign bottom summary UI, fix TDS display and missing txn_id column\n\n4.2 Commit 38fbc39\nTime: 18:53\nMessage: fix: resolve invoice duplicates, missing service charges, and dropdown reset bugs\n\n4.3 Commit 4ac4091\nTime: 16:25\nMessage: Refactor: Extract proforma invoice generation into a reusable modal component\n\n4.4 Commit ec110c5\nTime: 14:34\nMessage: feat: Add Balance Proforma and Payment History tabs in History Hub', '0', '0', 550, 0, '2026-06-30', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
