(12912, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'campaign', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Sub-Second OCR Engine Overhaul: Completely re-architected the Tesseract OCR implementation from a highly inefficient 60-pass loop down to a single persistent background worker. This monumental optimization slashed processing times from a sluggish 5 minutes down to an unprecedented 0.6 seconds per extraction.\nSelf-Healing Image Preprocessing Pipeline: Engineered an advanced, automated image correction system using the Sharp library. It dynamically detects EXIF orientation, auto-rotates inverted or skewed images, and applies a massive upscale-and-normalize filter to transform low-quality, blurry mobile uploads into crystal-clear inputs for flawless OCR accuracy.\nLabel-Agnostic Intelligent Parser: Developed a highly sophisticated heuristic parsing algorithm that completely eliminates the need for static labels like \"Name\" or \"Gender.\" The system now intelligently maps the spatial relationships of the text (such as locating the name proximally to the DOB) to flawlessly extract data from any unstructured Aadhaar layout.\nAggressive OCR Noise Rejection: Designed an impenetrable algorithmic shield to filter out OCR artifacts and garbled text (like \"bu ba P\"). By implementing strict minimum-character thresholds and fuzzy-logic matching (correctly identifying \"RAL\" as a corrupted \"MALE\"), the system guarantees only valid, pristine personal data enters the database.\nMulti-Dimensional Image Fusion: Built a seamless, state-of-the-art multi-image processing pipeline on the frontend. When a user uploads multiple images (e.g., front and back of the card) and triggers the extraction, the backend processes them in parallel, extracts fragmented data across all images, and perfectly fuses them into a single, complete profile instantly.\nBulletproof Server Architecture: Implemented robust backend guardrails that proactively intercept and reject unsupported formats like PDFs at the routing layer, ensuring the OCR engine never stalls and providing complete server stability under unpredictable user inputs.', '0', '0', 510, 0, '2026-07-01', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12913, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', '# Daily Task Report: DM-Calculator Invoice Architecture & Logic Fixes\n\nThis report outlines the comprehensive backend and frontend fixes deployed today to resolve structural calculation errors, UI state misalignments, and database synchronization issues across the invoice generation and management modules.\n\n## 1. Core Invoice Calculation & Payment Summary Restructuring\n\n**Issue:** The \"Previous Balance\" was being incorrectly added to the \"Invoice Total\" on fresh and subsequent proposal-based invoices, inflating the grand total. Furthermore, backend calculations were saving incorrect previous amounts during subsequent payment cycles.\n**Solution:**\n\n* **Backend (`proposalController.js`):** Rewrote the mathematical engine for tracking payments. Ensured the first payment strictly records `previous_amt` as `0`. For subsequent payments, the logic now fetches the true remaining balance (`total_amount - totalPastPayments`) to accurately set the `previous_amt` and `current_amt`.\n* **Frontend (`AdminInvoice.jsx`, `BDInvoice.jsx`):** Implemented a strict isolation layer using `isProposalInvoice`. Redesigned the Payment Summary UI to display a transparent mathematical breakdown: Invoice Total, Less Total Previous Payments, Outstanding Before This Payment, Gross Payments Received, and Outstanding Balance.\n* **Legacy Support:** Maintained the older rendering logic for legacy calculator-based invoices to prevent data breaking.\n* **Word Conversion Fix:** Resolved the parser bug that caused the total amount string to render as \"undefined Rupees\".\n\n## 2. Complimentary Services Display Isolation\n\n**Issue:** Complimentary service items were being calculated into the Grand Total, artificially inflating the final invoice amount despite being free items.\n**Solution:**\n\n* Extracted the \"Complimentary Services\" array from the main mathematical grid.\n* Rendered them into an isolated, distinct table strictly for visual representation.\n* Enforced a strict mathematical bypass ensuring these values are omitted from the final Grand Total and GST calculations.\n\n## 3. Dynamic Ads Budget Breakdown & Subtotal Synchronization\n\n**Issue:** The pricing summary section at the bottom of the invoice did not explicitly list the Google and Meta Ad Budgets, and the Ads Services table had been erroneously removed, causing a mismatch with the Proforma layout.\n**Solution:**\n\n* Restored the dedicated \"Ads Services\" table below the DM services grid.\n* Bound the final pricing summary rows (\"Google Ad Budget Inc GST\" and \"Meta Ad Budget Inc GST\") to the `showGoogleAd` and `showMetaAd` toggle states.\n* Ensured the Grand Total dynamically recalculates (DM Services + Ads Services) strictly based on the visibility state of these elements.\n\n## 4. Ads Campaign Budget Precision & Display Rounding\n\n**Issue:** Decimal fragments (`.97`, `.99`) were cluttering the UI in the Ads Campaign Budget Calculator, degrading the clean aesthetic.\n**Solution:**\n\n* Implemented display-level integer rounding (`Math.round()`) on the final rendered blocks for Budget, Charge, and Total rows in both `AdsCampaignCalculator.jsx` and `AdsCampaignCalciBD.jsx`.\n* Strictly preserved the underlying floating-point precision for internal component states to prevent integer drift and maintain 100% accuracy during 18% GST backend processing.\n\n## 5. GST State Resolution on Proforma History\n\n**Issue:** Generating a Non-GST Proforma worked correctly initially, but loading it from the `ProformaHistory` component forced an 18% GST calculation onto DM services.\n**Root Cause:** The history module was triggering a GST flag simply if `gst_amount > 0`. Since Ads services universally carry GST, this triggered a false positive for the entire invoice. Additionally, MySQL `BIT` fields were returning as `Buffer` objects, defaulting truthy evaluations.\n**Solution:**\n\n* Refactored the URL query parameter injection in `ProformaHistory.jsx` to bind strictly to the database\'s true `is_gst` flag rather than the aggregate tax amount.\n* Implemented rigorous type-checking across `AdminInvoice.jsx`, `ProformaManagerModal.jsx`, and `proposalController.js` to accurately parse MySQL Buffer objects into correct boolean states before evaluating tax matrices.\n\n## Modified Files\n\n* `client/src/Admin/AdminInvoice.jsx`\n* `client/src/BusinessDeveloper/BDInvoice.jsx`\n* `client/src/Admin/AdsCampaignCalculator.jsx`\n* `client/src/BusinessDeveloper/AdsCampaignCalciBD.jsx`\n* `client/src/Admin/ProformaHistory.jsx`\n* `client/src/Admin/components/ProformaManagerModal.jsx`\n* `server/controller/proposalController.js`', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-07-01', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
