(12925, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'new poroject', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Project: Siara Properties (Client & Admin Portals)\n\nDate: July 2, 2026\n\n????? 1. Dynamic Blogging System (Professional CMS Implementation)\nGoal: To replace static, hardcoded blog components with a robust, database-driven Content Management System (CMS) akin to WordPress/Medium.\n\nIntegrated React-Quill Editor (AddBlog.jsx & EditBlog.jsx): * Replaced the plain text area with a premium WYSIWYG editor supporting rich text (headings, bold, lists, blockquotes).\n\nCustom Image Upload Handler: Engineered a custom interceptor for Quill. When admins insert images, the system securely uploads the local file via Axios to the backend and dynamically injects the absolute server URL into the editor cursor range.\n\nComplete CRUD Functionality (AllBlogs.jsx): * Designed a sleek Admin data table for managing blogs.\n\nAdded seamless Edit capabilities, allowing the system to auto-populate existing HTML content and metadata into the editor, retaining existing assets unless explicitly changed.\n\nPremium Client Viewer Redesign (SingleBlogDynamic.jsx):\n\nTransformed the client-facing blog reading page into a distraction-free, premium layout using dangerouslySetInnerHTML.\n\nInjected scoped CSS styling to raw HTML: Enforced Cormorant Garamond for gold (#D4AF37) accented headings, elegant line heights for paragraphs, styled blockquotes, and responsive image scaling with soft shadows.\n\nAutomated Slug Routing: * Refactored the URL system to generate URL-friendly, regex-sanitized unique slugs from blog titles (e.g., my-premium-blog) for better SEO and cleaner navigation.\n\n????? 2. Backend Modularization & Storage Security\nGoal: Optimize the Node.js backend structure to cleanly handle multiple asset types and prevent server crashes.\n\nMulter Refactoring (utils/multerupload.js): * Extracted bulky image upload configurations out of propertyRouter.js and modularized them into a dedicated utils file.\n\nCreated separate upload instances: upload (for properties) and uploadBlog (for blog banner images), ensuring strict isolation of assets in uploads/blog/.\n\nDefensive File Deletion Protocol: * Upgraded the backend deleteBlog controller. Implemented fs.existsSync to proactively check if an image file exists before executing fs.unlinkSync(), successfully preventing fatal unhandled server crashes during deletions.\n\n???? 3. Global Authentication & Typography Overhaul\nGoal: Standardize the application’s design language (Cream/Terra/Ink) and drastically improve the user login experience.\n\nAuth UX/UI Glassmorphism: * Completely stripped outdated linear-gradient backgrounds and generic form elements from Login, Registration, and Forgot Password screens.\n\nImplemented premium dark-mode glassmorphism (backdrop-filter: blur(16px)) with Terra Gold (#b8895a) focus rings on inputs, matching Siara Properties\' elite brand identity.\n\nGlobal Typography Synchronization: * Embedded Cormorant Garamond (headings) and DM Sans (body text) directly into client/public/index.html. This eliminates FOUT (Flash of Unstyled Text) and ensures fonts load instantaneously across all views.\n\n???? 4. Global Architecture & Navigation Fixes\nGoal: Eliminate redundant code, enforce a Single Source of Truth for navigation, and resolve critical routing errors.\n\nNavbar Centralization: * Moved the premium Navbar.jsx component to the root App.js file (above the <Routes>).\n\nSafely deleted redundant <Navbar /> imports across 30+ child components, drastically reducing code repetition and ensuring the premium header is universally visible.\n\nDropdown UX State Resolution: * Replaced fragile CSS :hover logic on the user profile dropdown with a robust React state (onClick toggle). The menu now stays persistently open without vanishing when the mouse moves away.\n\nReact-Router Version Fix: * Resolved severe critical compilation crashes (undefined elements and missing export errors) by downgrading/locking react-router-dom to the stable v6 architecture and purging persistent Webpack caches.\n\nTechnical Note for QA/Testing: Due to extensive stylesheet and dependency updates, please ensure you perform a Hard Refresh (Ctrl + Shift + R) on the browser and ensure npm run build caches are cleared for local development testing', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-07-02', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
