(12930, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'campaign', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Deterministic DOM Layout Encapsulation\nEnclosed the auxiliary upload markup inside an IIFE-scoped conditional guard, preventing indiscriminate layout rendering across non-binary schema fields.\n2. ISO-8601 Temporal Lexical Alignment\nRefactored the raw OCR string token mapping with string splitting and zero-padded integer interpolation (.padStart). This normalizes legacy DD/MM/YYYY inputs into RFC-compliant temporal states to prevent native HTML5 input validation failures.\n3. Asynchronous Media Stream Lifecycle Synchronization\nIntegrated a non-TLS security check to prevent device-level camera thread crashes, alongside a custom React hook that dynamically binds resolving media streams to the canvas pipeline when the DOM node mounts.\n4. Client-Side Heap Protection & Raster Payload Downscaling\nPrevented mobile OS-level process terminations (page reloads) caused by volatile heap exhaustion by intercepting file input payloads, programmatically downscaling canvas dimensions to a 1600px boundary, and re-encoding the binary buffer.\n5. Production Bundle Compile-Time Verification\nExecuted Vite’s static compilation and tree-shaking compiler to confirm package bundle builds execute in under 463ms with zero runtime warning logs.', '0', '0', 393, 0, '2026-07-03', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(12931, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'new poroject', 'Development', 'FrontEnd ', 'Comprehensive Daily Task Report1. Development & Coding Updates (Siara Properties)Category: Frontend UI/UX, Code Maintenance, and Deployment TestingAdmin Panel Code Cleanup: Resolved terminal warnings by removing no-unused-vars (unused imports, Redux useDispatch calls, and variables) across multiple files including Contact_User.jsx, Interested_User.jsx, Registered_User.jsx, LoginAd.js, SoldProperties.jsx, SuggestedProperty.jsx, and AdminHome.jsx.Hero Section UI Enhancements: Improved readability for the \"Your Trusted Partner in Property\" text in Hero.jsx by updating the base color to dark brown (#7b4209), the animation color to caramel (#b8895a), and adding a soft white text-shadow for better contrast against the background.Property Types UI Polish: Replaced default mismatched blue icons in PropertyTypes.jsx with golden/brown brand colors, ensuring clean white transitions on hover/active states, and applied specific brand styling to the \"For Rent\" card.Footer WhatsApp Integration: Updated the WhatsApp icon in Footer.jsx to directly link to the provided number (+91 9243066371), automatically opening a chat in a new tab.Dynamic Copyright Implementation: Replaced the hardcoded footer year with a dynamic JavaScript date (new Date().getFullYear()) to ensure auto-incrementing copyright years.Contact Page Map Integration: Embedded a full-width, interactive Google Map in ContactPageNew.jsx pinpointing the exact office address (1815 Wright Town, Jabalpur), styled with rounded corners and a soft shadow to match the premium design.Local Build Testing: Successfully troubleshot and served the production builds locally (Client on port 5000, Admin on port 5001) to verify deployment readiness.2. Domain Research & Workflow AnalysisCategory: Product DiscoveryOphthalmology (Eye) Software Research: Successfully booked introductory appointments and meetings to deeply understand the workflows, requirements, and existing software solutions used in eye clinics/hospitals.3. System Architecture & Planning (IVF Module)Category: Backend & Frontend System Design (AI-Assisted)Role-Based Access Control Design: Established a strict role strategy introducing isolated user roles specifically for the IVF clinic, including IVF_Doctor, IVF_Nurse, IVF_Embryologist, and IVF_Receptionist.  Existing System Integration: Mapped out minimal-impact modifications for existing files (Sidebar.jsx, App.jsx, routes/index.js, dbJson.js) to seamlessly integrate the IVF section alongside the existing HMS without disrupting current workflows.  Database Structure Planning: Defined the JSON file initializations and helper functions required for managing IVF-specific entities like couples, cycles, stimulation, and lab embryos.  Backend Controller & Route Mapping: Designed the backend architecture to include 10 new distinct controller files (e.g., ivfPatientController, ivfLabController) and their corresponding route endpoints.  Comprehensive Screen Specification: Detailed the exact form fields, variable types, and HMS database connections required across 11 major frontend screens, covering everything from Couple Registration to Embryology Lab tracking and Pregnancy Follow-ups.  Implementation Roadmap: Developed a clear 11-phase execution sequence, ensuring logical development from basic role setup through to complex modules like Cryo Inventory and Dashboard reporting', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-07-03', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
