(12965, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Daily Task Report: Proposal Management, Invoice Layout, and System Enhancements\n\n## UI Enhancements\n\nUpgraded the standard popups for \"Send to Client\" and \"Mark Client Response\" in ProposalActions.jsx to a premium dark-mode theme using custom SweetAlert2 dialogs. Added dedicated visual cues, borders, and colors to match the core application aesthetic across different selection states.\n\nModified the workflow permissions to allow Business Developers to utilize the \"Send to Client\" trigger even if a proposal is actively in sent, changes, or rejected states, enabling continuous revisions without locking the interface.\n\n## Proposal Workflow and Status Management\n\nExpanded the PROPOSAL_STATUS_MAP on the frontend to include new status parameters for changes and rejected, and synced these updates directly with the backend MySQL database ENUM architecture to accurately track client interactions.\n\nConfigured proposalController.js to execute an automatic status reversion back to sent whenever a modified or updated document is dispatched to a client from an existing changes or rejected state.\n\nRefined the core filtering mechanics within ProposalHistory.jsx to systematically exclude records marked as draft, sent, changes, or rejected. This ensures the clean visibility of finalized items such as approved or proforma_generated entries within the centralized HistoryHub interface.\n\n## Email and PDF Attachment Integration\n\nRefactored the core Puppeteer rendering pipeline by extracting the document conversion mechanics from generateProposalPdf into a standalone, reusable createProposalPdfBuffer utility file.\n\nConfigured the sendProposalToClient module to assemble document streams straight into memory buffers for direct injection into sendEmails.js. This architecture replaces legacy temporary disk storage routines, eliminating residual file accumulation on the server filesystem.\n\nRedesigned the client-facing notification system by removing hardcoded links from the core layout. The new framework utilizes a card-style HTML email body that directs recipients to review the attached high-resolution document directly.\n\n## Invoice System Structural Updates\n\nIntegrated state-aware asset switching inside AdminInvoice.jsx and the backend drawing helpers using the isGST flag. The pipeline dynamically selects appropriate branding resources, alternating headers and digital signature graphics automatically depending on whether an invoice carries tax parameters.\n\nOverhauled the pdf-lib overlay layout matrix to ensure page components position correctly regardless of fluid text volumes. The updated layout constraints lock header images securely to the absolute page top and route footer components to the exact bottom margins of every generated page sheet, rather than rendering sequentially after body copy.\n\nResolved an asset rendering issue by introducing automated client-side canvas extraction. The download function loops through relative graphic nodes and serializes signatures into standalone base64 data strings, making them readable for headless Puppeteer instances operating outside localized network boundaries.\n\nFixed a text-truncation error within the final print styling context where localized string values were dropping inappropriately into secondary lines. Adjusted the CSS layout constraints and block sizing parameters across row elements to secure total counts on single, unbroken layout lines.\n\n## Configuration and Route Fixes\n\nUpdated structural environment parameters including local development URLs within the server env files to ensure consistent link formatting across testing deployments.\n\nAudited and aligned route targets across the billing layout files to ensure download methods reference correct backend endpoints, resolving endpoint mismatches during form processing.', '0', '0', 550, 0, '2026-07-06', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
