(12986, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Deep Analysis & Technical Task Report: Proforma Flow Standardization & UI Refactoring\n\nDate: July 07, 2026\n\n1. Executive Summary\n\nThe primary objective of today\'s work was to standardize the document generation workflow by making Proforma the mandatory intermediate stage before Invoice generation. Previously, the Instant flow generated Invoices directly, bypassing standard accounting practices. This workflow has now been restructured so that all document generation—whether from an Approved Proposal or a Manual/Instant flow—converges into the Proposal ? Proforma ? Payment ? Invoice pipeline.\n\nIn addition to the workflow restructuring, a detailed frontend code review and UI refactoring exercise was performed to eliminate duplicate logic, remove obsolete UI sections, simplify rendering logic, and improve maintainability without affecting business functionality.\n\n2. Database Architecture & Schema Enhancements\n\nThe revenue_engine.proposal_proforma table was enhanced to support both Proposal-generated and Manual (Instant) Proformas.\n\nSchema Changes\nModified proposal_id to allow NULL values for manually generated Proformas.\nAdded source_type (ENUM(\'proposal\', \'manual\')) to explicitly identify the origin of every Proforma.\nAdded source_id for future extensibility and source tracking.\nData Integrity\n\nThe existing snapshot-based architecture (pricing_snapshot, notes_snapshot, terms_snapshot) continues to preserve the exact state of a Proforma at generation time, ensuring the final Invoice always reflects the original approved document.\n\n3. Backend Implementation\n\nA dedicated backend pipeline was introduced for Manual (Instant) Proformas.\n\nNew Endpoint\n\nPOST /auth/api/calculator/saveDirectProforma\n\nResponsibilities include:\n\nAccepting client information and manually selected services.\nPerforming all financial calculations server-side.\nBuilding the standardized pricing_snapshot.\nSaving Terms & Conditions inside notes_snapshot.\nCreating a Proforma record with source_type = \'manual\'.\nMaintaining authentication and error handling through secure controller logic.\n4. Frontend Workflow Refactoring\nInstant Proforma Flow\n\nThe previous Instant Invoice flow has been converted into an Instant Proforma workflow.\n\nCompleted improvements include:\n\nRenamed \"Create Invoice\" flow to Instant Proforma.\nAdded dedicated Terms & Conditions support.\nReplaced direct Invoice generation APIs with the new Proforma endpoint.\nRedirected users directly to the generated Proforma preview.\nApproved Proposal Flow\n\nThe previous inline Proforma creation form has been replaced with the shared GenerateProformaModal component.\n\nThis standardizes features such as:\n\nGST Configuration\nPayment Details\nClient GST/PAN\nRemarks\nDate Selection\nNotes Management\n\nacross all Proforma generation methods.\n\n5. Frontend Code Review & UI Refactoring\n\nA detailed review of the Quotation rendering logic was performed to eliminate redundant code and simplify component maintenance.\n\nDuplicate Logic Identification\n\nThe following duplicate implementations were identified and reviewed:\n\nDuplicate calculation variables (grandTotalAds and grandTotal) performing identical computations.\nMultiple dead rendering blocks wrapped inside false &&, making them permanently unreachable.\nDuplicate DM Service Total calculations inside two separate IIFEs.\nRepeated Thumbnail, Content Posting and YouTube total calculations inside obsolete sections.\n\nThese redundancies were analyzed and cleaned where appropriate to improve readability and reduce unnecessary processing.\n\nComplimentary Service Refactoring\n\nThe complete Complimentary Services section was intentionally hidden from the rendered document while preserving backend data retrieval.\n\nThis approach keeps the implementation reversible for future business requirements without affecting existing APIs or database structures.\n\nRendering Logic Simplification\n\nThe Discount and Subtotal rendering section was simplified by:\n\nRemoving an unnecessary IIFE wrapper.\nEliminating repeated financial calculations.\nRendering Discount and Subtotal directly using already available component-level variables.\n\nThis reduced rendering complexity without changing business calculations.\n\nMinor Code Cleanup\n\nAdditional cleanup included:\n\nRemoving obsolete dead-code rendering blocks.\nIdentifying misleading section comments for future correction.\nReviewing calculation flow to ensure only actively used variables remain in production code.\n6. UI/UX Bug Fixes\n\nA critical stacking-context issue affecting the Proforma Generation Modal was investigated and resolved.\n\nRoot Cause\n\nThe parent animation container (ci-fadein) created a new CSS stacking context because of its transform animation.\n\nThis prevented the modal from overlaying the application\'s global navigation bar despite using a high z-index.\n\nSolution\n\nThe modal rendering was migrated to React Portal using createPortal(..., document.body).\n\nBenefits:\n\nEscaped the local stacking context.\nProperly overlays the global navigation.\nCorrect modal positioning on all screen sizes.\nCleaner architecture without CSS hacks.\n7. Conclusion\n\nToday\'s work significantly improved both the business workflow and frontend architecture.\n\nMajor achievements include:\n\nStandardized Proposal ? Proforma ? Payment ? Invoice workflow.\nAdded support for Manual (Instant) Proformas.\nEnhanced database traceability through source_type and source_id.\nUnified Proforma generation UI across the application.\nRemoved redundant frontend rendering logic and duplicate calculations.\nHidden obsolete Complimentary Service rendering while preserving backend compatibility.\nSimplified financial rendering logic.\nResolved modal layering issues using React Portals.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-07-07', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
