(12998, 120, 'Mohd Qaisar Moin', 'campaign', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'The Root Cause: Mobile devices suspend background tabs when launching resource-heavy camera and gallery interfaces, causing Vite\'s HMR WebSocket connection to drop. Upon returning to the tab, the reconnection forced a full page reload (window.location.reload()), wiping all form states.\nDouble-Layer Defense:\nFrontend: Server-side HMR was disabled (hmr: false in vite.config.js) and client-side HMR reload events were explicitly intercepted and blocked in main.jsx (return false).\nBackend: Nodemon configuration (nodemon.json) and Vite watcher custom filters were configured to completely ignore the Backend/uploads directory.\nHigh-Definition Capture & Pipeline: Replaced standard 1280px downscaled, lossy JPEG captures with 4K-supported native streams and lossless toBlob (1.0 maximum quality) uploading direct from memory to bypass compression constraints. Real-time Laplacian Variance blur detection warns users if quality is low.', '0', '0', 302, 0, '2026-07-08', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0),
