(13040, 85, 'Priti Bandewar', 'DOAGuru', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', 'Database Issue & Optimization: \nJo live aur local server pe database error aa raha tha, uski root cause (mysql2 configuration conflicts aur galat SQL queries) ko find karke resolve kiya. Pure letters module ke database connection ko optimize karke single clean Promise-based connection pe shift kiya.\n\nAPI & SQL Query Improvements:\nOffer letters aur Internship offers ke save, fetch aur update operations ki queries ko fix aur improve kiya. Update aur single-fetch APIs ki logic ko sahi kiya taki data bina kisi error ke database me save aur update ho.\n\nLocal & Live Server Testing: \nSabhi APIs ko local environment pe test kiya (Data creation & modification smoothly work kar raha hai). Live server ki schema compatibility aur errors ko inspect karke stable execution verify kiya.', '0', '0', 420, 0, '2026-07-10', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
(13041, 119, 'Ashish Dubey ', 'DM Calculator', 'Development', 'Front-end and Back-end ', '1. Proforma Invoice UI Restructuring\n\nThe Proforma Invoice was redesigned to make Ad Budget handling clearer and more user-friendly.\n\nRemoved the separate Ads Services table from the Proforma.\nMoved Show Google Ads Budget and Show Meta Ads Budget checkboxes from the Final Invoice to the Proforma Invoice (Quotation.jsx).\nPlaced these checkboxes above the Bank Details and Grand Total section as requested.\nWhen a checkbox is enabled, the corresponding Google or Meta Ad Budget appears as a separate line item inside the Grand Total Breakdown.\nGrand Total updates automatically whenever these checkboxes are enabled or disabled.\n2. Proforma Payment Recording Improvements\n\nThe payment recording process was enhanced to accurately capture ad budget payments.\n\nThe payment modal now supports recording Google Ad Budget and Meta Ad Budget separately instead of treating them as a single combined amount.\nValidation was added so users cannot save an Ad Budget payment without entering a valid amount.\nIf the project does not contain any Google or Meta Ads, the entire Ad Budget payment section remains hidden.\nIndividual Google and Meta Ad Budget amounts are stored separately for future invoice generation.\n3. Database Enhancements\n\nThe database structure was extended to support accurate ad budget tracking.\n\nAdded separate fields for:\nrealized_google_budget\nrealized_meta_budget\nThese fields are stored in payment records and carried forward into the final invoice.\nThis enables the system to distinguish between planned ad budgets and the actual amounts received from the client.\n4. Backend Logic Updates\n\nBackend APIs were updated to support the new payment workflow.\n\nPayment recording now saves Google and Meta Ad Budget amounts independently.\nDuring payment approval, these values are copied into the generated invoice.\nFinal invoices now use the actual recorded payment values instead of recalculating budgets from the project configuration.\n5. Invoice Billing Logic Fix\n\nA critical invoice calculation issue was resolved.\n\nPrevious Issue\n\nIf a project had:\n\nGoogle Budget = ?10,000\n\nand the client paid only:\n\nGoogle Budget = ?5,000\n\nthe generated invoice still displayed ?10,000, which was incorrect.\n\nRoot Cause\n\nThe invoice was incorrectly reading the total configured project budget from adsData because the invoice was still considered \"pending\". It ignored the actual payment values saved during the payment recording process.\n\nSolution\n\nThe invoice logic was updated to:\n\nUse the configured project budgets only while viewing a Proforma.\nUse the actual recorded payment values (realized_google_budget and realized_meta_budget) for Final Invoices.\n\nAs a result, invoices now always display the exact ad budget amount received from the client.\n\n6. Invoice UI Improvements\n\nThe invoice layout was reorganized to improve readability.\n\nRemoved Google Ad Budget Reimbursed and Meta Ad Budget Reimbursed from the upper billing breakdown.\nAdded these rows inside the Payment Summary section.\nPositioned them immediately above Gross Payments Received (Now) to clearly indicate that these are payment receipts rather than billable service charges.\n\nThis makes it clear that Ad Budgets are reimbursements and not part of the taxable service amount.\n\n7. Label & Text Updates\n\nSeveral invoice labels were improved for better clarity.\n\nUpdated Google Ad Budget ? Google Ad Budget Reimbursed.\nUpdated Meta Ad Budget ? Meta Ad Budget Reimbursed.\nUpdated Less: Project Value Deferred to Final Settlement Bill ? Less: Amount Deferred to Next Bill.\nUpdated Current Active Taxable Subtotal (Base for TDS) ? Net Taxable Value (This Bill).\nRemoved the unnecessary \"(This Bill)\" suffix where it was no longer required.\n8. Payment Summary Cleanup\n\nThe Payment Summary was simplified.\n\nRemoved duplicate Ad Budget information where necessary.\nEnsured Ad Budget reimbursements appear only in their appropriate section.\nPrevented duplicate display of the same values across different invoice sections.\n9. Dynamic Invoice Notes\n\nDynamic Terms & Conditions were enhanced.\n\nThe invoice now automatically displays contextual notes whenever applicable.\n\nAd Budget Note – Explains that Google and Meta Ad Budgets are pass-through reimbursements and not company revenue.\nTDS Note – Displays deducted TDS percentage, taxable value, deducted amount, PAN details, and Form 16A instructions.\nPrevious Invoice Note – Indicates that the invoice is a continuation of a previous invoice and references previously received payments.\nDeferred Amount Note – Explains that the deferred project value will be billed in a future invoice.\n\nThese notes appear automatically based on the invoice data and are also included in the generated PDF.\n\nOverall Result\n\nThe complete Ad Budget workflow has been redesigned.\n\nProforma now acts as a pricing and quotation document where Google and Meta Ad Budgets can be optionally included in the Grand Total.\nPayment Recording now captures the exact Google and Meta Ad Budget amounts received from the client.\nDatabase stores these received amounts separately for complete traceability.\nBackend transfers the recorded values directly into the invoice during payment approval.\nFinal Invoice displays only the actual received Ad Budget reimbursements instead of the total project budgets.\nThe invoice layout is cleaner, labels are more intuitive, duplicate information has been removed, and the entire billing workflow is now more accurate, transparent, and easier for both the company and clients to understand.', '0', '0', 500, 0, '2026-07-10', '', '', '', 0, '', 0),
